	"Author": "MagnoIia",
	"Description": "[size=3]After I released the buildings mod, I had an idea to also make matching fences too. So here we are.[/size]\n<br />\n<br />[size=3]Updates:\n<br />[/size]-\u00A0 21/04/2026\u00A0 - Added Alternative Textures version.\n<br />\u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0 \u00A0-\u00A0Fixed the gap between the gates and fences.\n<br />\n<br />[size=3]This mod replaces:[/size]\n<br />- wood fence, \n<br />- stone\u00A0fence, \n<br />- iron\u00A0fence,\n<br />- hardwood fence.\n<br />\n<br />[size=3]Recolors:[/size]\n<br />I made the seasonal overlays to match a few recolors so they wouldn't stand out from the rest of your game.\n<br />\n<br />[size=3]Seasonal vines:[/size]\n<br />There are a few color options for the vines, so you can match them to your game.\n<br />If you don't want them, you can disable them in the config options.\n<br />\n<br />[size=3]Snow in winter:[/size]\n<br />Just like the vines, snow also have a few color options and If you don't want it, you can disable it in the config.",
